WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.500
- [Narrator] This is a chip.

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.720
It's the brains of electronic devices,

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.170
laptops, smartphones, TVs,

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.190
and certainly the device

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:09.500
you're watching this video on right now.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.980
Almost half of these chips sold globally

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.050
by American firms like Qualcomm and Intel.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.770
But now China is racing to change that.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.280
The country has added almost $30 billion

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.520
into its own semiconductor companies,

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.550
like Chinese manufacturer, SMIC.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.940
- SMIC is China's hope to win
this tech race with the US.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.140
- [Narrator] SMIC is one of many

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.160
little known Chinese tech companies

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.060
that have seen their stocks rise

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.020
as the Trump administration
announced a number of moves

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.750
to effectively shut Chinese tech giants,

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.330
including TikTok and Huawei
out of the US market.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.970
- Huawei is something
that's very dangerous.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:49.710
- I mean, Washington's
attitude toward China,

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.033
particularly when it comes to technology

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:55.290
is that the two countries
need to separate.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.480
We could wind up with
two different ecosystems

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.910
when it comes to technology.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.550
- [Narrator] This separation process

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.410
has been called decoupling.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.120
So how are the US and China

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.300
trying to become more self-sufficient?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.960
And what does it mean for
tech giants in both countries?

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.320
- We cannot take the security risks

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.160
of any of those companies,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.890
including Huawei, which as
you know, we put a halt to.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.950
- [Narrator] Huawei and the
hugely popular video app, TikTok

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.380
have both been accused
of being potential tools

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.090
for Chinese espionage,

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:27.040
and have been labeled by
the US as a security threat.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.160
- We wanna see untrusted Chinese apps

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.730
removed from US app stores.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.840
President Trump has mentioned
impending action on TikTok,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.020
and for a good reason.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.470
- [Narrator] Both Huawei and TikTok

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.780
vehemently denied those allegations

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.970
and said they operate independently
from Chinese government.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.090
- And this administration has broadened

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.450
the notion of what national security is

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.910
way beyond any other administration.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.690
And when it comes to China,

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:53.740
they define national security as data,

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.220
all Chinese technology is suspect,

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.065
according to this administration.

00:01:58.065 --> 00:01:59.210
- [Narrator] As TikTok received threats

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.400
of being outright banned in the US

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.610
and the US government said
Huawei would be barred

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:06.600
from buying chips from the
US and other countries,

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.800
investment from China has
almost ground to a halt.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.540
- Chinese investment in the US
is down 90 some odd percent.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.410
- [Narrator] The restrictions
have also startled

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:17.090
a number of American companies,

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.860
which have been lobbying
hard against the changes.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.220
Huawei is a big client for corporations,

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.440
including Qualcomm and Intel.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.280
The likes of Microsoft's Bill Gates,

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.650
and Alibaba's Jack Ma have
said the recent escalations

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.360
are counterproductive for both sides.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.880
- American companies
supply parts to Huawei,

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.230
that may all go away, all of it.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:40.120
I mean, the Trump administration's message

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.960
to American companies
and European companies

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.890
that wanna do business
in China is don't do it,

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.000
come to the US.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.610
- [Narrator] So how is China responding?

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.530
Beijing announced it would no longer allow

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.550
its own artificial intelligence tech,

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.350
think facial recognition
and data processing,

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.803
to be exported without new licenses.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.850
While Washington and Beijing

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.430
are fighting on a number of fronts,

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:04.540
from Hong Kong to Taiwan
and the South China Sea,

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.920
tech has emerged as a strategic priority.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.470
That's where companies like SMIC come in.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:13.130
- China has had a long standing desire

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:17.530
to reduce Chinese companies
dependence on foreign supply.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:22.240
However, it's really not
until the Trump's trade war

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.700
that the Chinese leadership realized

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.740
that this is really serious,

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.840
we really need to put
our act together now.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.290
- [Narrator] China
launched its own version

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.870
of the NASDAQ last year, the STAR market,

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.190
and stocks there are soaring.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.770
It reflects how much investors
think companies can benefit

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:41.063
from the country's
quest for self-reliance.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.700
- Under Xi Jinping, there's a new slogan,

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.200
it's called domestic circulation.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.570
This esoteric slogan means
that China going forward

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:54.820
is going to prioritize its own companies,

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.020
its own markets and Chinese consumption.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.250
- [Narrator] Chips are
particularly important.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:03.230
China is the world's
biggest consumer of chips.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.630
It spends more on chips
than it does on oil,

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:09.570
and imported $300 billion
worth of chips last year.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:12.880
- Policy makers are using
SMIC as a role model

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.740
for other companies
with similar ambitions,

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:18.120
they're basically telling those companies,

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.570
we're willing to invest in
you, we're willing to help you,

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:25.270
but as long as you adhere
to the policy agenda.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.760
- [Narrator] Beijing is already touting

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.210
a number of successes.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.610
China's economy is forecast

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.620
to be the only major
economy to grow this year.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.930
And that's benefiting it's tech giants.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:38.960
Huawei, which is already a
global champion in 5G technology

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.920
became the number one
smartphone seller in July,

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.210
mostly, thanks to its domestic market,

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:47.350
where it sells over 70% of its phones.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.710
But ending its reliance on US technology

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:50.980
remains complicated.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.640
- We have a lot of really
smart engineers and scientists

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.520
on both sides of the Pacific.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.180
If they are not working together,

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.160
that will clearly retard innovation.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.810
- [Narrator] Huawei announced in 2019

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:04.620
that it can produce a
phone without US chips.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.213
Still, those substitute
parts of themselves made

00:05:07.213 --> 00:05:09.670
with American technology and tools,

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:11.600
and the administration has taken steps

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.340
to close the loophole.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.460
And if US regulation doesn't allow Huawei

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.430
to buy key components made with US tech,

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:21.960
Huawei may simply not be
able to produce its hardware.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.460
Analysts estimate that Huawei
stockpile of US components

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:27.750
will only last one or two years.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.710
Huawei has declined to
comment on its inventory.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:33.050
Huawei situation is seen as a confirmation

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:35.080
that despite heavy investment,

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:39.090
Chinese chip companies like
SMIC are still lagging behind.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:41.330
China is said to be about four years

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.313
behind the US and Taiwan.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.150
SMIC, which also uses
a lot of US technology,

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.050
has said it aims to
accelerate the development

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.240
of its own chip making capability.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.140
- China has been here before.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:56.630
It has been trying to catch
up with the US for decades.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:59.970
And it's not the first time
it has invested so heavily

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.980
in semiconductor industry.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:05.270
However, it still has a huge gap to fill,

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:07.280
and now time is running short.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.560
- [Narrator] And the US
is also making moves.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.400
Legislation is making its
way through the US Senate

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.060
that could pump an additional $37 billion

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.380
into American semiconductor manufacturing

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:19.080
and research and development.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.540
And whether or not Trump is reelected,

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.020
US actions aren't likely to stop.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.840
- I don't think that
a Biden administration

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.670
would take a fundamentally
different view toward China.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.450
China would still be the
number one competitor.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.480
There would still be issues,
you know, on human rights,

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.490
national security, technology.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:40.120
- No matter who's next in the White House,

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.530
this kind of inward
turning policy China has

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.080
is here to stay.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.500
China's leadership realizes

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:50.240
the US is no longer a reliable partner.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.610
- [Narrator] So after years
of escalating tensions

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:54.270
between the US and China,

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.330
the decoupling of their tech industries

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:57.820
will now likely continue.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.220
- I mean, what the US
at the moment is doing

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:03.110
is saying to the rest
of the world, choose,

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.330
you know, you're gonna go with us

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:05.780
or you're gonna go with them.

